\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Adaptive pickup $I_p^*$ for LL (left) and SLG (right) faults. Grey bars: setting produced by each estimator. Blue annotations: confidence score $\gamma $. The fixed relay does not adapt ($I_p = 1.00\,\text  {p.u.}$, $\gamma $ not applicable). Stage~1 produces a lower $I_p^*$ due to the biased $\hat  {I}_{ss}$ and lower confidence. The sequence estimator produces a higher, more accurate $I_p^*$ with significantly improved confidence, especially for SLG and LLG faults where Stage~1 either marginally accepts or rejects the update.}}{7}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:relay}{{7}{7}{Adaptive pickup $I_p^*$ for LL (left) and SLG (right) faults. Grey bars: setting produced by each estimator. Blue annotations: confidence score $\gamma $. The fixed relay does not adapt ($I_p = 1.00\pu $, $\gamma $ not applicable). Stage~1 produces a lower $I_p^*$ due to the biased $\hat {I}_{ss}$ and lower confidence. The sequence estimator produces a higher, more accurate $I_p^*$ with significantly improved confidence, especially for SLG and LLG faults where Stage~1 either marginally accepts or rejects the update}{figure.7}{}}
